# 1v1, cloud locks to the PC (BENCH-253), round 6: every per-robot line that locked on the cloud (95% low end above 0,
# live turn time; coverage/shards/locks.tsv) after round 5 (PR #870) ran, locked on 12 fresh PC seeds:
#   rh (RAM-14 heavy rammer dodge, off on master until this card holds it): Galaxy03 +1.4 (low +0.5), RammingC +1.0 (+0.4, 36 seeds),
#      Galaxy03 over 24 fresh cloud seeds; nanoPri left the card after 12 more seeds (+0.3, low -0.5 over 36)
#   dp (DIST-4 distance pin): Original pinned at 600 px +1.8 (+0.7)
#   sp2 (DODGE-6 shot-dodge planner, shot-dodge2 lines): SuperTracker +2.4 (+1.3), MilkyWay +0.8 (+0.5),
#      QuantumChromodynamics +1.46 (+0.63, 24 seeds),
#      BoxCar +1.89 (+1.11, 24 seeds), Arco +0.67 (+0.24, 24 seeds), YaroBot +0.84 (+0.16, 24 seeds),
#      Acero +1.6 (+0.9), ToNoone +2.65 (+1.8), Phoenix +0.85 (+0.05, 24 seeds), KomoriNinja +0.76 (+0.22, 36 seeds), ROBv203 +1.17 (+0.49, 36 seeds)
#   or (MOVE-47 steady orbit, off on master until this card holds it): GreenDragon +3.1 (+2.0, 24 seeds), DuelistNano +3.35 (+1.37, 24 seeds)
#   mt (SHIELD-17 shield add): Recrimpo +2.8 (+0.8), PointInLineRRAL +2.1 (+0.3, 36 seeds)
#   hl (MOVE-13 stop-and-start heat jitter): Roberto +0.96 (+0.37, 24 seeds)
#   gl (GUN-11 gun stack): EL33tGangstarr2 +0.65 (+0.03), Frederick +0.57 (+0.26), Polaris +1.06 (+0.56), each over 24 seeds
#   mtx0 (shield on, with its 150-damage battle exit off): NeophytePRAL +4.3 (+1.3)
#   rwl (MOVE-46 ram wait on a disabled enemy, off on master until this card holds it): One +1.22 (+0.68),
#      SavantVS +0.62 (+0.26), DengerousRoBatra +0.81 (+0.14), Smog +1.13 (+0.44), JGAP23423 +0.78 (+0.21), Rover +2.1 (+0.7), Pinkbot +0.8 (+0.4), GPBotA +0.7 (+0.3), ProjectNano +1.1 (+0.5), JGAP7958 +1.4 (+0.3), Experimental +1.33 (+0.85), Ambassador +0.44 (+0.07, 24 seeds), Piyane +2.0 (+0.8), X1 +1.4 (+0.06),
#      each over 24 fresh cloud seeds
#   DengerousRoBatra and EL33tGangstarr2 only just clear 0 over 24 cloud seeds; the PC decides them.
#   livematch  the released jar and BeepBoop 2.0 on the 31-robot panel at the live constant, read against live
#   lock       the 37 robots  c / aa / rh / dp / sp2 / rwl / gl / hl / mt / or / mtx0 (each lever arm built with only its own robots)   12 fresh seeds
#              from 43600, --cpu-constant live, in work/pc-locks6 (earlier rounds' battles stay in work/pc-locks to -locks5)
#   gate       each robot judged on its own arm only (lock_prep.py --restrict); it keeps its line where the 95% low end
#              is above 0 (mode_table.py --margin 0)
# Leigh starts it once the PC is free (one card at a time, from master):
#   git checkout master && git pull
#   .\queue.ps1 run pc-locks --fresh        (or  ./queue.sh run pc-locks --fresh)
#   --fresh because round 5 left this plan's queue state marked complete; an interrupted round 6 resumes without it.
# One bench queue, RoboRumble workers at 0, 16 workers, truth log off. 4884 lock battles (37 robots, 11 arms, 12 seeds), about 125 minutes
# with the live-match check.
#
# Why it should win (the PC card rule of 2026-11-03):
#   - Per-opponent tailoring: every line names one robot; every other robot, team and melee play bit for bit as master.
#   - Diagnosis first (coverage/shards/pbL/README.md; shard C easy-band lane; truth logs against BeepBoop 2.0):
#     rh: BeepBoop scores 6 to 10 points a robot more than we do against these nano rammers. RAM-2's escape runs from
#     round 3 and its RAM-5 shot dodge carries it (off: -10.4 a robot); the dodge's weight curve on cloud seeds peaked at
#     120 px a hit aim (30 -1.5, 60 master, 120 +1.8, 240 +0.3, 480 +1.1), and 120 held over 24 fresh seeds on these three.
#     dp: BeepBoop fights Original beyond 500 px where we fight at 350-500; the pin holds us at 600 px (shard C).
#     sp2: SuperTracker and MilkyWay aim exactly where a lateral-velocity model puts us (0.91 and 0.57 of their bullets);
#     the shot-dodge planner cut MilkyWay's matched-bullet hits from 0.040 to 0.006 a shot (shard A, move/route.md).
#     rwl: field traces put 26% of our hit damage after the enemy is disabled, against 9-13% for BeepBoop and Saguaro,
#     because END-2 rams straight into the disabled enemy's last bullets; waiting until none of its waves is surfable
#     keeps the surf on them (shard B, PR #875). As a global rule it was level, so it is per opponent.
#     Rover, Pinkbot, GPBotA (ram-wait sweep): after they are disabled we take 108, 86 and 98 bullet damage a battle against BeepBoop's 42, 8 and 0;
#     ProjectNano and JGAP7958 (shard M sweep) carry 152 and 93 a battle more post-disable damage than BeepBoop takes.
#     sp2 (QuantumChromodynamics): 52% of its shots sit on the linear intercept; BeepBoop takes 0.3% hits, we take 2.3%.
#     gl: we hit EL33tGangstarr2 30% of shots against BeepBoop's 51% and Saguaro's 62%; the gun stack lifts our aim.
#     On Frederick and Polaris BeepBoop's per-bullet hit rate leads ours by 0.15 with post-kill shots dropped (shard G gun census).
#     sp2 (BoxCar): a linear-intercept shooter (37% of its shots); we take 450 bullet damage a battle against BeepBoop's 120 (shard C).
#     sp2 (Arco, YaroBot): non-rammers held at 385-430 px whose aim the planner reads (shard G, move/planG.md).
#     sp2 (Acero, KomoriNinja, ROBv203): shard A's planner predictor picked them from the class sort; ROBv203 fights at 271 px with no ram.
#     mt: Recrimpo leaks hits with the shield off; the shield add held +2.8 where shield with exit off (mtx0) lost -3.1 (shard A).
#     sp2 (ToNoone, Phoenix): head-on guns (Phoenix 99% head-on); the planner steps off the head-on line (shard C easy band).
#     or: Saguaro orbits GreenDragon-like guns without stopping; two-thirds of their bullets aim near head-on and our flat surf
#     spends 24% of waves there taking half its hits; dropping the stop option and adding reversal hysteresis held +3.1 (shard A, PR #887).
#     hl: Roberto does 207 bullet damage a battle to us against 123 to BeepBoop; stop-and-start breaks its aim (shard C).
#     mtx0: the shield alone was level on NeophytePRAL (-0.7) because the 150-damage exit turns it off and 143 hits
#     leak after; with the exit off, damage taken fell from 15.8 to 3.1 a round (shard M, move/shield-M.md).
#   - Every robot passed the cloud lock bar first; round 4 held 5 of 6 (#866), round 5 held 4 of 6 (#870).
# Stop rules (docs/bench/watch.md): the watcher's A/A rule needs 10 robots read in both c and aa, which this 37-robot
# lock reaches only near its end (shuffled jobs), so no aa stop rule is set; aa is read in the gate (multiarm.py prints aa against c). The card halts on 30 failed
# battles, an arm scoring nothing in 8, 60+ skipped turns a battle over the last 24, or no battle in 30 minutes. The
# live-match step stops the card if the PC no longer scores us and BeepBoop as live does (tools/live_match.py exit 3).
# ALERT opens an issue for Leigh on any stop.
# Bank: the owning cloud thread adds the gate's lines on this card's results PR. Nothing is released by the card.
set V = 3.23
set P = --parallel 16 --no-truth-log --failed-ok
set C = --skip-build --skip-fetch --rounds 35 --cpu-constant live --child-heap 2G
set W = work/pc-locks6
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set ALERT = lgriffin

prep | git checkout -q master && mkdir -p bisect work && (cd .. && mvn -q -DskipTests package) && cp ../hadur-robot/target/hadur117.Hadur_${V}.jar bisect/ && bash ./build-ablation.sh aa && python3 tools/lock_prep.py plans/locks-pick.tsv panel-locks.txt plans/pc-locks.arms ${W}-prep && bash ${W}-prep/build.sh && for a in rh dp sp2 rwl gl hl mt or mtx0; do test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}$a.jar || exit 1; done && bash tools/fetch_live_jar.sh && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-r31.txt && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set livematch-bb.txt && test -f opponents/kc.mega.BeepBoop_2.0.jar && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-locks.txt && mvn -q compile

livematch | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-r31.txt --seeds 2 --seed-base 21700 --arms plans/livematch.arms --out work/pc-livematch-rel-live --label pc-locks-livematch --shuffle-jobs && python3 tools/live_match.py work/pc-livematch-rel-live/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/pc-locks6-livematch.md
  after: prep
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: stall 30m

lock | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-locks.txt --seeds 12 --seed-base 43600 --arms ${W}-prep/lock.arms --out ${W} --label pc-locks --shuffle-jobs
  after: livematch
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: skips 60 over 24
  stop: stall 30m

gate | python3 ../data/tools/multiarm.py ${W}/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks6-lock.md && python3 tools/lock_prep.py --restrict ${W}/arms.tsv ${W}-prep ${W}/arms-picked.tsv && python3 ../data/tools/mode_table.py ${W}/arms-picked.tsv --margin 0 --out-tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks6-lock-pick.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks6-lock-pick.md && python3 tools/per_robot.py ${W}/arms-picked.tsv --arms rh dp sp2 rwl gl hl mt or mtx0 --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks6-lock-per-robot.md --out-tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks6-lock-per-robot.tsv
  after: lock

pr | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-locks6-results "1v1 cloud locks, round 6 (37 robots from the field shards) locked on 12 fresh PC seeds" ${OUT}/pc-locks6-livematch.md ${OUT}/*_pc-locks6-*.md ${OUT}/pc-locks6-lock-per-robot.tsv $(find ${OUT} -maxdepth 1 -name 'pc-locks6-lock-pick.tsv' -size +0c)
  after: gate
